Subject: Tweak: mirror match
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509

In Domination's captain select, a captain one team has picked is greyed out
and the other team cannot pick him: OnCaptainPointerEnter and
OnCaptainPointerPress refuse him, and RefreshCaptainImages shows his
disabled portrait. The title screen's demo matches avoid the same captain
too. With "Mirror match" enabled, offline Domination keeps that captain lit
and available, so both teams can have the same captain. The Road to the
Striker Cup and online or LAN matches keep the original rule.

CharacterLoader has a branch for one captain on both teams, which the
retail game never reaches: it dresses the away team's captain and sidekicks
in the captain's away kit. The tweak completes it:

- The away goalie wears the away kit as well.
- Mario, Luigi, Wario and Waluigi have no away kit on the disc; the branch
  would have asked for textures that do not exist. Their away kit is made as
  the home kit loads (the port's src/platform/away_kits.cpp): the kit
  texture of the captain's model and the team textures of his goalie and
  sidekicks are recoloured into a white kit with red trim for Mario, sky blue
  for Luigi, blue for Wario and orange for Waluigi, and registered under the
  away kit's name. Sidekick and goalie team textures are compared with the
  same texture of two other teams, read from the disc, so only their team
  colour changes.
- On the field the away team's colour is its kit's (the player indicators
  and the defensive play overlay). In the menus (captain and sidekick select,
  Choose Sides, the pointers, the holograms) and for the Mega Strike hand,
  the away team takes the away kit's colour and textures where the game has
  a complete away kit, the one a captain wears against a captain of his
  colours (Bowser, Bowser Jr., Daisy, Diddy Kong, Donkey Kong, Petey and
  Yoshi). Peach's blue kit has no sidekick portraits or Mega Strike hand, so
  she wears it on the field only. NeedsAlternateColour and GetTeamColour
  cannot tell two teams of one captain apart, so these hooks pass the side.
- Choose Sides shows both teams' captain as holograms. An impostor's render
  targets are named after its character (ImpostorCharacter), so the away
  hologram would draw into the home one's targets, and destroying both
  would free them twice. A character already shown gets targets of its own.

A captain on both teams otherwise loads like a sidekick kind on both teams,
which the game allows: one template, and a sound bank slot per team.

